<title>GERMANY: Viag sees 97 sales up, slight profit rise.</title>
<headline>Viag sees 97 sales up, slight profit rise.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>German diversified utility Viag AG said on Friday it expected group sales to grow to more than 45 billion marks ($26.4 billion) in 1997 from 42.45 billion marks in 1996.</p>
<p>Chief Executive Georg Obermeier told the group's annual news conference the company would at least match, but possibly exceed, earnings before and after tax in 1997.</p>
<p>In 1996, group net profit totalled 1.06 billion marks while pre-tax profit was 2.35 billion marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.702 German Marks)</p>
